EXACT PRODUCT PLATEAUS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  n=14: 5/11 = 5/11
  n=16: 34/33 = 34/33; 35/33 = 35/33
  n=18: 1 = 1
  n=16 phase step: (35/33)/(34/33) = 35/34

PROOF GRAMMAR
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  boundary witness:      ArchGap=0, Debt>0
  positive-gap witness:  ArchGap>0, any Debt
  exported debt branch:  ArchGap*Debt >= c(n) > 0
  counterexample target: ArchGap=0 and Debt=0

A product lower bound belongs to the exported branch, not to the
initial boundary branch.  It says that if a repair shrinks the
Archimedean gap, 2-adic endpoint debt must grow quickly enough that
the pair cannot converge to (0,0).
